# NOTE 1

One thing to flag honestly: this IAM setup uses long-lived access keys, which is the same pattern we deliberately avoided in your GitHub Actions pipeline with OIDC. For a Raspberry Pi sitting on your home network there's no equivalent of OIDC federation, so static keys are the practical choice here — but it's worth being able to explain that tradeoff in an interview too: "OIDC where the platform supports it, scoped IAM credentials with rotation where it doesn't."


